---
/**
 * Stránka pro modelky.
 *
 * Dva důvody, proč existuje, a oba jsou skutečné:
 *
 * 1. **Ventil.** Publikujeme o reálných lidech víc než jen výpis: kde ještě
 *    vysílají a (od konce srpna) kdy je vídáme online. To druhé je informace
 *    o rutině konkrétní osoby a bez možnosti odhlášení by to bylo přes čáru.
 *    Opt-out se dělá kódem v room subjectu, takže je **self-service a ověřitelný**
 *    — do subjectu svého pokoje může psát jen ona.
 * 2. **Odkazy.** Odkazy jsou strop tohohle webu (DR 13) a nekupují se. Když si
 *    odznak dá do bia dvě stě modelek, je to dvě stě odkazů z cizích domén,
 *    které si nikdo neobjednal.
 *
 * Stránka **nic neslibuje**, co nemáme: žádné „propagujeme tě", žádné placené
 * pozice. Popisuje, co o ní publikujeme a odkud to máme.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { FACETS, MODEL_PAGES } from '../lib/data';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL, approx } from '../lib/seo';

const networks = FACETS.networks.length;
const profiles = MODEL_PAGES.length;
const title = `For cam models – Your eCamx page, badge and opt-out | ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description = `What eCamx publishes about you, how to get a free link back to your `
	+ `profile page, and how to remove yourself in one line — no email needed.`;
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'For models' }]} />

	<h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold sm:text-3xl">For cam models</h1>
	<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-ink-400">
		eCamx lists {approx(profiles)} performers from {networks} cam sites in one place.
		If you broadcast on any of them, you already have a page here — you did not sign up
		for it and you can remove it. This page explains both.
	</p>

	<section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="what-h">
		<h2 id="what-h" class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold">What we publish about you</h2>
		<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
			<li><strong>What the site's own feed says</strong> — your nickname, the room
			subject you set, your tags, and whatever else that platform makes public
			(age, country, HD flag; each site publishes a different subset).</li>
			<li><strong>Our own observations</strong> — the days we saw you live, the highest
			viewer count we recorded, and the two-hour windows in which we usually find you
			online. Nothing about who you are; only when your room was open.</li>
			<li><strong>The same nickname on another site</strong>, when we find one. We say
			it is a <em>name</em> match and never claim it is the same person — nicknames are
			not reserved across cam sites.</li>
			<li><strong>Nothing else.</strong> No recordings, no screenshots we keep, no
			private details, and no data from anywhere except the sites' own public feeds.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-400">
			Thumbnails are hot-linked from the cam site's own CDN — we do not copy or store
			images.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="out-h">
		<h2 id="out-h" class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold">Removing yourself — one line, no email</h2>
		<p class="mb-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
			Put this anywhere in your <strong>room subject / status</strong> on the cam site:
		</p>
		<p class="mb-3 rounded border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900 px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-white">
			ecamx-out
		</p>
		<p class="mb-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
			We read room subjects every two hours, so your profile disappears at the next
			refresh — from the listings, from the search index and from the schedules. You can
			take the line out again afterwards; nothing is kept in the meantime. We ask for it
			this way on purpose: <strong>only you can edit your own room subject</strong>, so
			nobody can remove a competitor and you do not have to prove anything to us.
		</p>
		<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
			<strong>XLoveCam is the exception.</strong> Its feed does not include room subjects
			at all, so the code cannot reach us. Write to
			{' '}<a href="mailto:info@ecamx.com" class="text-accent underline">info@ecamx.com</a>
			{' '}from any address and say which profile — we will not ask you to prove it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="badge-h">
		<h2 id="badge-h" class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold">If you would rather be found</h2>
		<p class="mb-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
			Your eCamx page works as one link that does not die when you switch sites: it shows
			whichever of your rooms is live right now, so a fan who follows you here sees which
			site to open — even on a day you switched. Some performers put it in a bio next to
			their socials.
			It is free, there is nothing to claim, and we get nothing from it beyond the visit.
		</p>
		<p class="mb-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
			Your page address is <code>{SITE_URL}/live/your-nickname/</code> — search your name
			in the {' '}<a href="/finder/" class="text-accent underline">finder</a> to get the exact one.
		</p>
		<p class="mb-2 text-sm text-ink-400">Badge for your bio (copy and paste):</p>
		<pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900 p-4 text-xs text-ink-200"><code>&lt;a href="{SITE_URL}/live/your-nickname/"&gt;&lt;img
  src="{SITE_URL}/badge-ecamx.svg" alt="Watch me live on eCamx" width="160" height="32"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>
		<p class="mt-3">
			<img src="/badge-ecamx.svg" alt="Watch me live on eCamx" width="160" height="32" />
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="fair-h">
		<h2 id="fair-h" class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold">The part most directories leave out</h2>
		<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
			We earn a commission when someone we sent to a cam site buys tokens there. That is
			the whole business model, and it means our interest is in sending you real viewers
			rather than in keeping them here. It also means we have no reason to rank you by
			anything other than what the data says — there is nothing to buy on this site and
			no paid placement to sell.
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>
